1
00:00:01,634 --> 00:00:06,206
Even if it was true,
this is not the place to talk about it!

2
00:00:06,339 --> 00:00:11,277
Director, as you can see,
I'm perfectly healthy. Please believe me.

3
00:00:14,280 --> 00:00:16,683
Please don't cast me aside.

4
00:00:17,317 --> 00:00:18,351
Daimon.

5
00:00:19,686 --> 00:00:23,990
You've made a cancer patient
out of Torii in front of everyone.

6
00:00:25,325 --> 00:00:26,459
What for?

7
00:00:28,395 --> 00:00:29,929
Do you want to bring him down?

8
00:00:29,996 --> 00:00:30,964
MICHIKO DAIMON

9
00:00:31,031 --> 00:00:33,133
It's because we don't have
a moment to spare, of course.

10
00:00:33,199 --> 00:00:35,635
SURGERY DEPARTMENT II CHIEF
TAKASHI TORII

11
00:00:39,839 --> 00:00:40,974
Professor Torii.

12
00:00:42,675 --> 00:00:44,144
Let me operate on you.

13
00:00:46,413 --> 00:00:48,214
I will not fail.

14
00:00:50,283 --> 00:00:51,785
HOSPITAL DIRECTOR
RYUNOSUKE BUSUJIMA

15
00:00:52,919 --> 00:00:54,754
Ridiculous. Stop that nonsense.

16
00:00:55,221 --> 00:00:56,523
Torii, you--

17
00:00:56,589 --> 00:00:59,426
It's a groundless allegation.
Director, everyone,

18
00:00:59,726 --> 00:01:02,095
I'm sorry, but I must ask you to leave.

19
00:01:02,695 --> 00:01:04,397
I don't have much time
until the conference.

20
00:01:04,864 --> 00:01:06,166
Are you still talking about that?

21
00:01:06,232 --> 00:01:08,701
I don't have a minute to spare
on this absurd conversation.

22
00:01:09,969 --> 00:01:11,071
Understood.

23
00:01:18,645 --> 00:01:21,081
If you're a surgeon,
you know better than anyone else

24
00:01:21,147 --> 00:01:23,516
that it'll be too late unless
you get operated on right now.

25
00:01:29,789 --> 00:01:31,157
You don't understand at all.

26
00:01:33,893 --> 00:01:38,965
Even if I had cancer,
as your absurd diagnosis suggests,

27
00:01:39,799 --> 00:01:40,900
I won't have the surgery.

28
00:01:41,701 --> 00:01:42,569
Why?

29
00:01:43,036 --> 00:01:45,138
Presenting my research paper

30
00:01:45,738 --> 00:01:50,376
at the international conference
comes first more than anything.

31
00:01:50,844 --> 00:01:52,112
More than your own life?

32
00:01:53,446 --> 00:01:55,048
Yes, that's right.

33
00:01:57,584 --> 00:01:58,885
HIDEKI KAJI

34
00:01:58,952 --> 00:02:00,687
MAMORU HARA

35
00:02:02,555 --> 00:02:04,157
You heard me. Now get out.

36
00:02:05,024 --> 00:02:06,259
- Hara.
- Yes.

37
00:02:07,494 --> 00:02:09,229
Get this analyzed right away.

38
00:02:11,197 --> 00:02:12,132
Will do.

39
00:02:26,479 --> 00:02:29,516
Professor Torii's CT's here, right?
Show me.

40
00:02:34,154 --> 00:02:35,155
Director.

41
00:02:36,356 --> 00:02:43,062
As Daimon said, this is
definitely hilar bile duct cancer.

42
00:02:43,129 --> 00:02:45,665
Stage 3.

43
00:02:45,732 --> 00:02:48,601
Please make him stop working
on the international conference

44
00:02:48,668 --> 00:02:50,870
and direct him to get surgery immediately.

45
00:02:51,037 --> 00:02:53,306
That's up to Torii to decide.

46
00:02:54,174 --> 00:02:57,544
If his priority is his reputation
as a medical scientist,

47
00:02:58,044 --> 00:02:59,913
I cannot stop him.

48
00:03:01,047 --> 00:03:05,985
In other words, whether it's
too late or not, you don't care.

49
00:03:06,920 --> 00:03:07,787
Stop it.

50
00:03:10,790 --> 00:03:13,626
I'm not that inhuman.

51
00:03:14,561 --> 00:03:17,297
You may not believe it,
I'm a devout Christian.

52
00:03:19,165 --> 00:03:20,500
That doesn't matter.

53
00:03:20,567 --> 00:03:24,771
The only thing you want
is fame for the hospital.

54
00:03:28,007 --> 00:03:29,275
Let's keep this...

55
00:03:29,876 --> 00:03:31,844
between you and I.

56
00:03:32,512 --> 00:03:36,015
- I'll tell her to keep silent, too.
- Yes.

57
00:03:37,050 --> 00:03:40,320
From today, I want you all to stay here

58
00:03:40,386 --> 00:03:42,155
and help professor
with his research paper.

59
00:03:42,222 --> 00:03:45,558
I know you're all busy,
but let's unite as Surgery Department II

60
00:03:45,625 --> 00:03:48,461
- and complete his medical paper.
- Understood, if Dr. Hara insists.

61
00:03:48,528 --> 00:03:49,429
HIKARU MORIMOTO

62
00:03:49,495 --> 00:03:50,496
I'll help, too.

63
00:03:50,563 --> 00:03:52,232
Let's make the conference a success.

64
00:03:52,699 --> 00:03:53,800
You got that?

65
00:03:54,234 --> 00:03:55,068
You help, too.

66
00:03:56,135 --> 00:03:57,136
Why?

67
00:03:57,837 --> 00:04:00,740
For now, finishing the research paper
is top priority.

68
00:04:02,375 --> 00:04:05,078
And in order to have him
concentrate on getting treatment.

69
00:04:07,113 --> 00:04:09,782
Daimon, just this one time.
It's for Professor's sake.

70
00:04:11,551 --> 00:04:12,952
I'm not doing it.

71
00:04:13,953 --> 00:04:16,990
- Listen, you--
- Excuse me. I have to go now.

72
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:28,434
Michiko.

73
00:04:30,536 --> 00:04:31,604
Long time, no see.

74
00:04:34,107 --> 00:04:37,010
It's been a long time, Dr. Hijikata.

75
00:04:37,310 --> 00:04:38,811
MAIN HOSPITAL PROFESSOR
IKUYA HIJIKATA

76
00:04:39,679 --> 00:04:41,247
So, you're back from Cuba.

77
00:04:47,053 --> 00:04:48,087
Why are you here?

78
00:04:48,354 --> 00:04:49,656
I'm thinking the same.

79
00:04:50,156 --> 00:04:53,059
Director Busujima called me over
to Surgery Department II.

80
00:04:55,194 --> 00:04:56,696
What a drag.

81
00:04:57,897 --> 00:05:01,734
<i>This is the story</i>
<i>of a lone wolf woman doctor.</i>

82
00:05:02,835 --> 00:05:03,803
Excuse me.

83
00:05:05,738 --> 00:05:08,474
Professor Hijikata.
We've been waiting for you.

84
00:05:09,309 --> 00:05:11,311
Nice to meet you. It's a pleasure.

85
00:05:14,480 --> 00:05:18,718
Well, Professor Hijikata.
I'm glad to see you here.

86
00:05:18,785 --> 00:05:20,286
The surgery took longer than expected.

87
00:05:20,353 --> 00:05:21,821
- I'm sorry for being late.
- It's fine.

88
00:05:21,888 --> 00:05:24,557
<i>University hospital</i>
<i>medical offices were losing power,</i>

89
00:05:25,058 --> 00:05:26,926
<i>and even medicine,</i>
<i>dealing with life and death,</i>

90
00:05:26,993 --> 00:05:30,196
<i>plunged into an era</i>
<i>where the law of the jungle prevailed.</i>

91
00:05:33,566 --> 00:05:37,704
<i>To fill the critical shortage</i>
<i>in the medical field are the freelance.</i>

92
00:05:38,871 --> 00:05:41,174
<i>In other words, a lone wolf doctor.</i>

93
00:05:41,240 --> 00:05:42,075
SECRETARY
AI OKUMURA

94
00:05:44,043 --> 00:05:46,312
<i>For example, this woman.</i>

95
00:05:47,046 --> 00:05:51,517
<i>She hates groups, she hates authority,</i>
<i>and she hates constraints.</i>

96
00:05:52,051 --> 00:05:56,189
<i>Her weapons are her specialty license</i>
<i>and her skill to work her way up.</i>

97
00:05:56,989 --> 00:05:59,492
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

98
00:06:00,393 --> 00:06:01,728
<i>Also known as...</i>

99
00:06:02,462 --> 00:06:03,896
<i>Doctor X.</i>

100
00:06:10,803 --> 00:06:13,606
DOCTOR X SURGEON MICHIKO DAIMON
EPISODE 7

101
00:06:17,410 --> 00:06:21,013
Then when you're done transitioning
over at the main hospital,

102
00:06:21,214 --> 00:06:22,715
I look forward to working with you.

103
00:06:22,782 --> 00:06:24,217
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

104
00:06:28,988 --> 00:06:30,223
SURGERY DEPARTMENT II
ACTING CHIEF

105
00:06:30,289 --> 00:06:31,557
My pleasure.

106
00:06:31,624 --> 00:06:32,925
Professor Hijikata.

107
00:06:35,595 --> 00:06:37,697
<i>Oh, really? Ikuya Hijikata came?</i>

108
00:06:37,764 --> 00:06:38,998
<i>He went to study in Chicago...</i>

109
00:06:39,065 --> 00:06:39,899
KANEKO TERAYAMA

110
00:06:39,966 --> 00:06:42,435
<i>...from Totei University Medical Office,</i>
<i>and became a professor</i>

111
00:06:42,502 --> 00:06:44,537
<i>of liver transplant at the age of 38.</i>

112
00:06:44,604 --> 00:06:46,406
His career is blossoming

113
00:06:46,472 --> 00:06:48,975
and he has long legs
and he's good-looking.

114
00:06:49,108 --> 00:06:51,043
It doesn't look good for Professor Torii.

115
00:06:51,244 --> 00:06:55,014
But if Mr. Torii ends up doing well
at the conference in Paris,

116
00:06:55,081 --> 00:06:56,349
won't he turn things around?

117
00:06:56,416 --> 00:07:01,354
If so, Mr. Torii will be
the Surgery Chief at the main hospital.

118
00:07:01,721 --> 00:07:04,724
If he fails, he'll be banished
to the countryside.

119
00:07:04,791 --> 00:07:08,261
Either way, the seat
for Surgery Chief will open up.

120
00:07:08,327 --> 00:07:11,864
Busujima wants
to put Hijikata in that seat.

121
00:07:12,265 --> 00:07:16,803
I heard he's marrying the daughter
of a professor at the main hospital.

122
00:07:16,869 --> 00:07:18,971
A reverse Cinderella.
He's an accumulation of ambition.

123
00:07:19,038 --> 00:07:19,872
AKIRA KANBARA

124
00:07:20,540 --> 00:07:23,509
Mr. Torii doesn't stand
a chance after all.

125
00:07:23,976 --> 00:07:25,978
That's how it is.

126
00:07:26,312 --> 00:07:28,247
Not doing well?

127
00:07:28,848 --> 00:07:31,484
No pep at all... Michiko?

128
00:07:31,784 --> 00:07:33,386
You're awfully quiet tonight.

129
00:07:33,453 --> 00:07:36,789
That aside, he's going to die
if he doesn't have surgery soon.

130
00:07:36,856 --> 00:07:38,224
Who is?

131
00:07:38,291 --> 00:07:40,827
Choosing research papers
and fame over life.

132
00:07:42,428 --> 00:07:43,830
Everyone's gone mad.

133
00:07:45,698 --> 00:07:47,400
<i>Ron. </i>It's a winner.

134
00:07:47,867 --> 00:07:50,203
Nine lanterns!

135
00:07:50,269 --> 00:07:51,471
Michiko.

136
00:07:51,604 --> 00:07:58,578
<i>Tonight again, thank you</i>

137
00:08:07,887 --> 00:08:08,721
Ligation is done.

138
00:08:08,788 --> 00:08:10,022
- Metzen.
- Yes.

139
00:08:11,691 --> 00:08:12,859
Auto suture.

140
00:08:45,358 --> 00:08:47,693
Professor, you should take a break.

141
00:08:50,096 --> 00:08:51,297
I don't have time for that.

142
00:08:52,532 --> 00:08:53,699
<i>- Scalpel.</i>
<i>- Yes.</i>

143
00:08:54,166 --> 00:08:55,368
- Monopolar.
- Yes.

144
00:09:20,359 --> 00:09:21,360
Done.

145
00:09:28,100 --> 00:09:30,102
Gentlemen, you've all worked hard.

146
00:09:34,307 --> 00:09:37,109
Professor, you're the one who worked hard.

147
00:09:38,277 --> 00:09:39,445
You've worked hard.

148
00:09:40,413 --> 00:09:42,481
How many surgeries do I have today?

149
00:09:46,552 --> 00:09:47,620
Professor?

150
00:09:47,753 --> 00:09:51,290
Please cancel your trip to Paris
and get surgery immediately.

151
00:09:52,959 --> 00:09:54,860
Don't ever treat me like an invalid.

152
00:09:59,298 --> 00:10:00,800
Don't ever treat me like an invalid.

153
00:10:03,936 --> 00:10:05,471
I'm sorry, I fell asleep.

154
00:10:10,776 --> 00:10:12,645
Professor, are you not feeling well?

155
00:10:13,346 --> 00:10:14,280
Well.

156
00:10:14,714 --> 00:10:17,116
No, Professor hasn't been
getting much sleep and he's tired.

157
00:10:19,018 --> 00:10:20,620
Is the research paper done?

158
00:10:24,790 --> 00:10:26,425
SENDING
TRANSMISSION COMPLETED!

159
00:10:27,126 --> 00:10:30,196
All right. I can attend
the international conference.

160
00:10:33,366 --> 00:10:34,967
Professor Torii, congratulations!

161
00:10:35,034 --> 00:10:36,602
- Thank you.
- Congratulations!

162
00:10:36,669 --> 00:10:38,537
- Thank you.
- Congrats!

163
00:10:40,039 --> 00:10:41,374
Thank you.

164
00:10:41,440 --> 00:10:47,613
Professor, the day has finally come.
This is from Director Busujima.

165
00:10:50,082 --> 00:10:52,652
Have a safe trip!

166
00:10:53,119 --> 00:10:55,221
Thank you. Yes, thank you.

167
00:10:55,988 --> 00:10:57,423
I'm counting on you while I'm away.

168
00:10:57,490 --> 00:11:00,826
- Yes, have a safe trip.
- I'm off, then.

169
00:11:00,893 --> 00:11:02,628
- Good luck.
- Thank you.

170
00:11:12,171 --> 00:11:13,139
Professor Torii.

171
00:11:15,141 --> 00:11:17,843
- Have a safe trip.
- Thank you.

172
00:11:21,047 --> 00:11:22,548
Oh, crap. It's the professor's wife.

173
00:11:22,615 --> 00:11:23,683
What? His wife?

174
00:11:24,150 --> 00:11:25,785
- Hide her.
- Why?

175
00:11:25,851 --> 00:11:28,621
Just hide her! Dr. Shiraki, go!

176
00:11:29,488 --> 00:11:32,692
Ms. Okumura, Dr. Daimon's calling
for you. Come with me for a minute.

177
00:11:32,758 --> 00:11:36,562
- I'll miss my flight.
- You'll be fine! It won't take long.

178
00:11:36,629 --> 00:11:37,763
- I'll be off now.
- Yes.

179
00:11:37,830 --> 00:11:39,732
Dr. Daimon has urgent business.

180
00:11:39,832 --> 00:11:41,133
- I'm here.
- What?

181
00:11:42,001 --> 00:11:43,035
And I didn't ask for her.

182
00:11:44,303 --> 00:11:47,440
- What's going on?
- They're covering you up.

183
00:11:52,678 --> 00:11:55,214
Dear. Thank goodness,
I caught you in time.

184
00:11:56,115 --> 00:11:58,984
You didn't have to come see me off.

185
00:11:59,151 --> 00:12:03,422
An amulet. I got it at Minakami Shrine.

186
00:12:04,623 --> 00:12:06,826
"Realization of earnest wishes."
Thank you.

187
00:12:06,892 --> 00:12:09,595
If you fail this time,
there won't be a next time.

188
00:12:09,662 --> 00:12:10,663
NANAKO TORII

189
00:12:10,730 --> 00:12:11,564
Keep that in mind.

190
00:12:14,066 --> 00:12:14,934
I'm off, then.

191
00:12:17,570 --> 00:12:18,604
Have a safe trip.

192
00:12:20,372 --> 00:12:23,743
- I'll be fine from here.
- Take care, have a safe trip.

193
00:12:24,176 --> 00:12:25,144
Take care, sir.

194
00:12:34,887 --> 00:12:38,290
- Professor! Are you all right?
- Dear!

195
00:12:38,357 --> 00:12:39,358
Are you all right?

196
00:12:39,458 --> 00:12:40,726
- Move!
- Dr. Daimon.

197
00:12:42,027 --> 00:12:42,862
Dear!

198
00:12:42,962 --> 00:12:44,296
- Stretcher!
- Yes.

199
00:12:45,197 --> 00:12:46,098
Professor?

200
00:12:46,165 --> 00:12:48,100
- Take his vitals.
- Yes.

201
00:12:48,968 --> 00:12:50,336
Establish an IV route.

202
00:12:50,402 --> 00:12:53,372
Never mind. I have to go to Paris.

203
00:12:53,439 --> 00:12:55,040
You're a patient already.

204
00:13:01,547 --> 00:13:04,383
Upper abdominal area CT.
In 1 millimeter slice, three phases.

205
00:13:04,583 --> 00:13:06,485
Create a 3-D vascular image, too.

206
00:13:15,661 --> 00:13:19,532
Ms. Daimon. Thank you for your hard work.

207
00:13:19,932 --> 00:13:21,066
You may go now.

208
00:13:23,102 --> 00:13:26,405
Those unaffiliated with the university
must refrain from further involvement.

209
00:13:26,472 --> 00:13:27,473
Why?

210
00:13:28,073 --> 00:13:31,010
Because we don't want outsiders
to know the professor's condition.

211
00:13:31,677 --> 00:13:33,779
You blurt out
what you're thinking, don't you?

212
00:13:34,847 --> 00:13:36,448
Come on, get out!

213
00:13:40,319 --> 00:13:42,021
Make sure you examine him thoroughly!

214
00:13:49,428 --> 00:13:50,296
Wait!

215
00:13:56,402 --> 00:13:58,604
He's dying, isn't he?

216
00:14:00,272 --> 00:14:02,808
- We're running some tests now.
- He's going to die, isn't he?

217
00:14:05,144 --> 00:14:07,646
I don't care if he has cancer or whatever.

218
00:14:08,380 --> 00:14:12,551
But I need him to live much longer.

219
00:14:14,353 --> 00:14:16,255
Our son is still in junior high.

220
00:14:16,322 --> 00:14:19,525
For him to attend medical school,
we need the money.

221
00:14:27,233 --> 00:14:28,334
I see.

222
00:14:37,810 --> 00:14:43,616
That's the situation, so, gentlemen,
please act accordingly.

223
00:14:45,184 --> 00:14:47,319
- Yes.
- I understand.

224
00:14:47,786 --> 00:14:48,721
I understand.

225
00:14:49,622 --> 00:14:50,589
Yes, sir.

226
00:15:00,900 --> 00:15:03,202
We'll now begin the emergency conference.

227
00:15:04,370 --> 00:15:05,371
Excuse me.

228
00:15:06,705 --> 00:15:10,276
Professor Torii, himself,
will be attending today

229
00:15:10,743 --> 00:15:13,846
and we'll report the test results
and discuss surgical procedures.

230
00:15:15,981 --> 00:15:17,516
Since I'm a doctor myself,

231
00:15:17,917 --> 00:15:20,586
I'd like to know about
my condition in detail.

232
00:15:20,886 --> 00:15:22,454
I'll be sitting in.

233
00:15:23,622 --> 00:15:26,525
Without further ado,
who would you like to be your surgeon?

234
00:15:33,866 --> 00:15:36,001
Kaji, please.

235
00:15:38,671 --> 00:15:40,773
Please put up the image
of the test results.

236
00:15:47,913 --> 00:15:53,085
Cancer has not invaded the left
intrahepatic bile duct or the portal vein.

237
00:15:54,019 --> 00:15:54,954
Stage 2.

238
00:15:55,454 --> 00:15:58,424
Condition is worsening,
but removal is possible.

239
00:15:59,491 --> 00:16:01,527
I see. That's a relief.

240
00:16:02,161 --> 00:16:03,062
I'll leave it to you.

241
00:16:03,128 --> 00:16:06,198
- Yes, I'll do my very best.
- Objection.

242
00:16:08,434 --> 00:16:12,204
According to my diagnosis,
it's no longer possible to remove it.

243
00:16:12,604 --> 00:16:13,839
What are you talking about?

244
00:16:14,039 --> 00:16:17,142
There's no disorder in the blood vessels
or the left intrahepatic bile duct.

245
00:16:17,476 --> 00:16:19,178
There's no problem
in liver function either.

246
00:16:19,244 --> 00:16:22,948
Professor, we've determined
removal is definitely possible,

247
00:16:23,015 --> 00:16:24,516
so please put your mind at ease.

248
00:16:29,588 --> 00:16:33,425
This angiography...
Is this really Professor Torii's?

249
00:16:33,492 --> 00:16:35,894
- Yes, it is.
- Of course, it is.

250
00:16:35,961 --> 00:16:36,829
Daimon,

251
00:16:37,296 --> 00:16:41,633
please stop making remarks
that may inflame the patient's anxiety.

252
00:16:41,700 --> 00:16:44,703
Aren't doctors
obligated to tell the truth?

253
00:16:46,305 --> 00:16:51,844
Then let's hear your diagnosis.

254
00:16:51,910 --> 00:16:56,115
It's past the point of removal
by general surgical procedures.

255
00:16:56,915 --> 00:17:00,519
Since cirrhosis has developed,
you'll need a transplant.

256
00:17:01,320 --> 00:17:04,289
Otherwise, you have six months to live.

257
00:17:11,930 --> 00:17:13,065
Six months to live.

258
00:17:14,199 --> 00:17:15,234
Professor Torii.

259
00:17:16,635 --> 00:17:19,138
The only option we have
is a living donor liver transplant.

260
00:17:20,172 --> 00:17:22,875
Let's begin the search
for a donor at once.

261
00:17:28,013 --> 00:17:29,948
Don't you have a human heart?

262
00:17:30,082 --> 00:17:31,650
Given such a grim prognosis,

263
00:17:31,717 --> 00:17:34,853
anyone would feel hopeless
and lose the will to fight the disease!

264
00:17:34,920 --> 00:17:35,754
HIROMI JONOUCHI

265
00:17:35,821 --> 00:17:38,190
Does Professor Torii
really have only six months to live?

266
00:17:38,257 --> 00:17:41,060
So, he was writing his paper
until it got to that point.

267
00:17:41,860 --> 00:17:43,128
Let me ask you, then.

268
00:17:43,529 --> 00:17:47,533
If you were in his place,
do you want to be lied to?

269
00:17:49,101 --> 00:17:49,935
That's...

270
00:17:51,470 --> 00:17:54,273
There's no way we can tell him the truth.

271
00:17:54,339 --> 00:17:57,676
We're not talking about a layman
who can be deceived until the end.

272
00:17:57,976 --> 00:18:00,746
Professor Torii is a scientist
specializing in cancer.

273
00:18:11,190 --> 00:18:12,024
I spilled.

274
00:18:14,726 --> 00:18:18,063
Come to think of it,
for your first surgery,

275
00:18:18,130 --> 00:18:20,365
you did an appendectomy on me.

276
00:18:22,334 --> 00:18:23,402
Did I?

277
00:18:23,969 --> 00:18:26,138
Don't tell me you forgot.

278
00:18:26,572 --> 00:18:29,374
You lacked surgical skills
from back then, too.

279
00:18:30,042 --> 00:18:31,543
All residents lack skill.

280
00:18:32,744 --> 00:18:34,880
There's a limit to it.

281
00:18:34,947 --> 00:18:36,882
It was a normal appendectomy,

282
00:18:37,082 --> 00:18:41,120
but I have a 5 centimeter scar,
and look at this.

283
00:18:42,121 --> 00:18:43,222
It's jagged.

284
00:18:45,090 --> 00:18:48,427
With a scar like this, you probably
thought no one would marry me,

285
00:18:48,494 --> 00:18:50,529
so you felt responsible
and married me, didn't you?

286
00:18:53,031 --> 00:18:55,901
- What is it?
- No.

287
00:18:56,802 --> 00:19:01,540
I was wondering why you always
wore high panties like that.

288
00:19:03,041 --> 00:19:04,843
Well, sorry about that.

289
00:19:15,087 --> 00:19:17,489
Dr. Hijikata, please shake my hand.

290
00:19:19,725 --> 00:19:20,826
Where is...

291
00:19:21,927 --> 00:19:24,163
<i>Apparently, he was brought over</i>
<i>to replace Professor Torii.</i>

292
00:19:24,229 --> 00:19:26,365
Professor Hijikata's our next Chief?

293
00:19:29,401 --> 00:19:31,703
Don't you think it's too well-scripted?

294
00:19:33,071 --> 00:19:36,074
Yeah, being that
Professor Torii's still alive.

295
00:19:36,141 --> 00:19:38,810
I refuse to acknowledge
the new Surgery Chief.

296
00:19:44,516 --> 00:19:47,252
Professor Hijikata,
this is the medical office.

297
00:19:48,687 --> 00:19:52,257
I'm Hijikata, taking Professor Torii's
place while he's under medical care.

298
00:19:52,724 --> 00:19:54,293
- Nice to meet you.
- Yes, nice to meet you.

299
00:19:54,593 --> 00:19:56,528
- Nice to meet you.
- A pleasure.

300
00:19:57,362 --> 00:19:58,230
Ms. Michiko Daimon.

301
00:19:59,531 --> 00:20:01,667
Please get together for me
this week's surgery schedule

302
00:20:01,733 --> 00:20:03,435
and the patients' medical records.

303
00:20:03,835 --> 00:20:05,137
I'm not doing it.

304
00:20:05,837 --> 00:20:06,672
What?

305
00:20:12,077 --> 00:20:13,579
My working conditions.

306
00:20:15,347 --> 00:20:17,516
Helping out Professor and so on,

307
00:20:17,616 --> 00:20:20,786
I'll not do anything that can be done
without a medical license.

308
00:20:25,324 --> 00:20:26,925
You haven't changed at all.

309
00:20:27,626 --> 00:20:30,896
Professor, here are the surgery
schedule and medical records.

310
00:20:30,963 --> 00:20:31,930
Thank you.

311
00:20:35,300 --> 00:20:36,602
So cool.

312
00:20:38,604 --> 00:20:41,740
Hey, I thought you weren't
going to acknowledge him.

313
00:20:42,808 --> 00:20:46,979
Come to think of it, you were
the medical staff at Totei University.

314
00:20:47,412 --> 00:20:50,582
Then do you know
Professor Hijikata from back then?

315
00:20:52,651 --> 00:20:53,752
Hey...

316
00:20:55,053 --> 00:20:57,456
you were dating an elite like him?

317
00:20:57,756 --> 00:21:01,426
- That's hard to believe.
- And then you were ditched.

318
00:21:04,896 --> 00:21:07,866
His wife's in the room
and I can't get near him.

319
00:21:10,502 --> 00:21:11,637
Ms. Okumura,

320
00:21:13,171 --> 00:21:17,142
can you give half your liver to Professor?

321
00:21:17,276 --> 00:21:18,243
What?

322
00:21:18,310 --> 00:21:20,212
He'll be in trouble
if we don't find a donor soon.

323
00:21:20,279 --> 00:21:24,416
You have to get your stomach cut.
I can't. Besides, it sounds painful.

324
00:21:24,483 --> 00:21:26,451
He won't even divorce his wife.

325
00:21:29,821 --> 00:21:30,922
I thought so.

326
00:21:32,357 --> 00:21:36,828
<i>...surgical society meeting this year</i>
<i>is both overwhelmed and delighted...</i>

327
00:21:36,895 --> 00:21:38,430
How are you feeling?

328
00:21:45,671 --> 00:21:47,372
I guess you wouldn't be feeling good.

329
00:21:48,807 --> 00:21:51,943
I heard Hijikata came as the Acting Chief.

330
00:21:52,811 --> 00:21:57,049
From the time he was my assistant,
he was good at winning favor.

331
00:21:57,949 --> 00:22:03,455
In other words,
Director Busujima has cast me aside.

332
00:22:04,022 --> 00:22:05,057
More importantly,

333
00:22:05,590 --> 00:22:08,460
talk to your wife about
the living donor liver transplant.

334
00:22:09,761 --> 00:22:14,333
No, that wife of mine
will never give me her liver.

335
00:22:14,399 --> 00:22:16,234
Still, please ask her anyway.

336
00:22:19,571 --> 00:22:22,007
I'm tired. Let me be by myself.

337
00:22:34,953 --> 00:22:36,621
MASTER FOUNDATION

338
00:22:36,688 --> 00:22:38,390
THE HOPKINS MASTER PRIZE 2012

339
00:22:52,504 --> 00:22:54,406
- Professor Torii.
- Are you all right?

340
00:22:55,574 --> 00:22:57,709
Professor, don't do anything rash.

341
00:23:00,212 --> 00:23:03,582
<i>...and Takashi Torii from Japan.</i>

342
00:23:03,648 --> 00:23:04,750
Professor?

343
00:23:06,485 --> 00:23:07,352
I did it.

344
00:23:09,154 --> 00:23:10,222
Take a look!

345
00:23:10,489 --> 00:23:13,892
<i>Now, we gratefully praise</i>
<i>the combination therapies</i>

346
00:23:14,292 --> 00:23:17,696
<i>for K-RAS wild-type colorectal cancers,</i>

347
00:23:18,130 --> 00:23:21,266
<i>submitted by Professor Takashi Torii</i>

348
00:23:21,867 --> 00:23:26,738
<i>from Teito Medical University</i>
<i>and we also strongly nominate</i>

349
00:23:27,205 --> 00:23:31,977
<i>this marvelous work for the Hopkins</i>
<i>Master Prize in Medical Research.</i>

350
00:23:32,077 --> 00:23:34,980
Professor, you did it!

351
00:23:35,380 --> 00:23:36,515
Congratulations!

352
00:23:38,116 --> 00:23:41,453
<i>We're afraid that Professor Torii</i>
<i>is absent from the conference today,</i>

353
00:23:41,920 --> 00:23:44,856
<i>but his terrific research</i>
<i>is greatly admired.</i>

354
00:23:44,990 --> 00:23:49,327
Good Lord.
Professor Torii's research paper...

355
00:23:51,897 --> 00:23:54,199
This is an unexpected achievement.

356
00:23:54,866 --> 00:23:57,669
Professor Torii will be a star overnight.

357
00:23:58,570 --> 00:24:02,441
Looks like I won't be wanted here
even if I came.

358
00:24:04,576 --> 00:24:05,477
No.

359
00:24:08,947 --> 00:24:12,217
There's a big job waiting for you.

360
00:24:13,018 --> 00:24:14,019
A big job?

361
00:24:15,053 --> 00:24:15,921
What can that be?

362
00:24:24,529 --> 00:24:29,134
Good day. Thank you. Quiet, please.

363
00:24:29,234 --> 00:24:31,503
- Congratulations on the nomination.
- Thank you very much.

364
00:24:31,570 --> 00:24:33,772
Please let us interview Professor Torii.

365
00:24:33,839 --> 00:24:37,042
We'll keep it short.
Just a comment or two.

366
00:24:37,609 --> 00:24:40,612
In order to complete his research paper,

367
00:24:40,679 --> 00:24:44,449
Professor Torii overexerted himself,
and he's currently under the weather.

368
00:24:44,516 --> 00:24:47,319
However, just this once,
we'll make an exception,

369
00:24:47,385 --> 00:24:49,554
and give permission for an interview.

370
00:24:52,724 --> 00:24:56,428
Congratulations on your nomination
for the Master Award.

371
00:24:56,795 --> 00:24:58,797
- Thank you.
- Congratulations!

372
00:25:01,266 --> 00:25:06,471
How does it feel to be chosen as
a candidate for such a prestigious prize?

373
00:25:07,405 --> 00:25:09,140
I'm still just a candidate.

374
00:25:10,041 --> 00:25:13,245
However, I'm glad.

375
00:25:13,311 --> 00:25:17,148
As a doctor, how do you feel about
the fact that your own research

376
00:25:17,215 --> 00:25:19,551
was recognized by the world?

377
00:25:21,152 --> 00:25:23,722
Performing surgery is not my forte.

378
00:25:24,589 --> 00:25:27,125
While practicing medicine,
I've never been called a great doctor.

379
00:25:27,425 --> 00:25:30,962
However, by the fact
that this medical paper was recognized,

380
00:25:32,464 --> 00:25:35,901
there's a new possibility
that many patients may be saved.

381
00:25:39,237 --> 00:25:41,273
Colon cancer surgery
and combined scientific therapy

382
00:25:41,573 --> 00:25:44,776
cross over as it relates
to K-RAS genetic mutation...

383
00:25:49,981 --> 00:25:53,585
This research,
for which I risked everything...

384
00:25:57,155 --> 00:26:00,058
Professor? Professor!

385
00:26:00,725 --> 00:26:02,627
- Professor!
- Professor!

386
00:26:02,827 --> 00:26:03,695
Hang in there!

387
00:26:08,199 --> 00:26:10,835
State of shock from acute
circulatory collapse from liver failure.

388
00:26:11,136 --> 00:26:12,404
Epinephrine, one ampule.

389
00:26:12,470 --> 00:26:15,206
He wasn't just suffering from fatigue?

390
00:26:15,373 --> 00:26:17,776
Shut up! You're all in the way. Get out!

391
00:26:18,376 --> 00:26:19,377
We're very sorry.

392
00:26:19,444 --> 00:26:21,513
NO VISITORS

393
00:26:22,147 --> 00:26:24,549
Good grief. At a time like this.

394
00:26:25,617 --> 00:26:27,786
We'll be in trouble if you die now.

395
00:26:30,121 --> 00:26:31,056
Sorry.

396
00:26:33,224 --> 00:26:34,526
Get Daimon here.

397
00:26:38,396 --> 00:26:39,798
Get Daimon here.

398
00:26:40,065 --> 00:26:42,334
I'm right here. What is it?

399
00:26:44,703 --> 00:26:46,004
I hate Hijikata.

400
00:26:47,606 --> 00:26:49,474
He's the last guy I want operating on me.

401
00:26:49,841 --> 00:26:51,109
What are you talking about?

402
00:26:54,346 --> 00:26:56,348
What is it? Do you want to sit up?

403
00:27:40,625 --> 00:27:42,093
Daimon, you do the surgery.

404
00:27:46,665 --> 00:27:48,099
You don't make mistakes, right?

405
00:27:51,503 --> 00:27:52,370
Yes.

406
00:27:59,177 --> 00:28:00,412
I'm counting on you.

407
00:28:16,027 --> 00:28:18,863
Daimon, what do you want,
barging in like this?

408
00:28:20,832 --> 00:28:22,767
Please have this processed.

409
00:28:27,439 --> 00:28:28,506
Excuse me.

410
00:28:32,510 --> 00:28:35,046
Director, this is from Professor Hijikata.

411
00:28:36,114 --> 00:28:37,215
Dr. Daimon.

412
00:28:38,717 --> 00:28:41,853
Then please process this.

413
00:28:47,392 --> 00:28:49,394
You are?

414
00:28:50,495 --> 00:28:52,063
I'm Morimoto from Surgery Department II.

415
00:28:52,530 --> 00:28:53,898
Morimoto.

416
00:28:54,499 --> 00:28:58,670
Are you aspiring to be a researcher?
Or clinical practice?

417
00:29:02,707 --> 00:29:05,510
Clinical practice. I'm still an assistant,

418
00:29:05,610 --> 00:29:08,480
but I'm hoping to be a surgeon
who can perform flawless surgeries.

419
00:29:08,813 --> 00:29:12,417
All right. I'll let
Professor Hijikata know so that

420
00:29:12,584 --> 00:29:14,652
you can use a scalpel as soon as possible.

421
00:29:19,124 --> 00:29:20,191
Thank you.

422
00:29:22,427 --> 00:29:23,261
Wait a minute.

423
00:29:25,964 --> 00:29:26,798
Yes.

424
00:29:49,654 --> 00:29:54,359
TEITO MEDICAL'S GENIUS
MASTER NOMINEE, PROFESSOR TORII

425
00:29:54,425 --> 00:29:56,661
<i>"Can the team of doctors</i>
<i>at Teito Medical University</i>

426
00:29:56,928 --> 00:29:59,864
save the life of Master Award
Nominee Professor Torii?"

427
00:30:00,331 --> 00:30:04,936
Six months to live. That means he won't
last until the award is announced.

428
00:30:05,904 --> 00:30:10,041
Now that we have this,
if we let Torii die before he's awarded,

429
00:30:10,108 --> 00:30:12,243
Teito Medical University's reputation
will be lost.

430
00:30:12,310 --> 00:30:15,146
Yeah, it's a matter of life or death
for the main hospital as well.

431
00:30:15,613 --> 00:30:18,049
Hey, put your mind at ease.

432
00:30:19,083 --> 00:30:23,788
The scenario for the surgery
is already in place.

433
00:30:24,689 --> 00:30:30,261
However, the main character isn't
Professor Torii, but the other star.

434
00:30:36,201 --> 00:30:38,536
I think I'll have you grill
an abalone for me today.

435
00:30:38,603 --> 00:30:39,504
Certainly.

436
00:30:48,513 --> 00:30:51,716
Laparotomy by Mercedes-Benz incision.

437
00:30:51,783 --> 00:30:56,855
The important thing is to carefully
and quickly treat the hepatic vein.

438
00:30:56,921 --> 00:31:00,725
If you let it bleed, you may end up
with mass hemorrhage on your hands.

439
00:31:00,959 --> 00:31:03,428
You need to be perfectly in tune
with your assistant.

440
00:31:03,995 --> 00:31:05,430
You're good as always.

441
00:31:06,364 --> 00:31:09,367
Makes me want to do
a joint surgery with Akira again.

442
00:31:09,434 --> 00:31:12,804
That would be impossible.
My medical license was revoked.

443
00:31:13,705 --> 00:31:14,539
What?

444
00:31:15,039 --> 00:31:17,208
License revoked?

445
00:31:18,243 --> 00:31:21,980
So... what did you do?

446
00:31:23,414 --> 00:31:27,185
If you want to learn from the master,
don't ask useless things.

447
00:31:27,652 --> 00:31:29,454
Another important thing is...

448
00:31:30,555 --> 00:31:33,825
remove the cancer in one lump.

449
00:31:33,892 --> 00:31:38,396
And save much of the remaining
hepatic vein and blood vessels.

450
00:31:39,964 --> 00:31:43,534
<i>We'll now begin the open conference.</i>

451
00:31:43,601 --> 00:31:46,804
The patient is Chief of Surgery
Department II at this hospital

452
00:31:46,871 --> 00:31:50,108
recently chosen as
a Master Award candidate for his work

453
00:31:50,174 --> 00:31:54,012
on K-RAS genetic mutation,
Professor Takashi Torii

454
00:31:54,679 --> 00:31:55,513
48 years old.

455
00:31:55,813 --> 00:31:58,216
This surgery is anticipated
around the world,

456
00:31:58,783 --> 00:32:01,019
so those of you from the press,
we thank you for coming.

457
00:32:03,922 --> 00:32:05,423
I'm Busujima, the Director.

458
00:32:06,057 --> 00:32:08,960
The donor of the liver for this surgery

459
00:32:09,560 --> 00:32:12,263
is the person who quietly
and devotedly supported

460
00:32:13,398 --> 00:32:16,834
Professor Torii and his research.
His wife.

461
00:32:19,671 --> 00:32:21,072
I'm Nanako Torii.

462
00:32:23,141 --> 00:32:25,576
And the primary surgeon is...

463
00:32:27,545 --> 00:32:29,781
Professor Ikuya Hijikata.

464
00:32:33,351 --> 00:32:35,453
Photographers, please come to the front.

465
00:32:35,887 --> 00:32:38,356
I'm sure all of you already know this,

466
00:32:38,790 --> 00:32:43,194
but Professor Hijikata is
a global authority on liver transplant.

467
00:32:43,261 --> 00:32:45,330
Back when I was a resident,

468
00:32:45,430 --> 00:32:47,732
Professor Torii taught me surgery
from the fundamentals.

469
00:32:48,266 --> 00:32:51,970
I wished I could repay him in any way
and so I decided to take it on.

470
00:32:52,036 --> 00:32:55,773
Wait a minute. The primary surgeon is me.

471
00:32:55,873 --> 00:32:59,310
- Daimon.
- She's gone mad again.

472
00:32:59,377 --> 00:33:01,279
I have the Director's approval as well.

473
00:33:01,346 --> 00:33:04,148
- Director, is this true?
- Daimon.

474
00:33:04,949 --> 00:33:06,651
- What are you talking about?
- Excuse me,

475
00:33:07,452 --> 00:33:09,420
but are you with the medical staff here?

476
00:33:09,487 --> 00:33:11,990
No. That person there
is a freelance surgeon.

477
00:33:12,056 --> 00:33:16,227
But Professor Torii gave me
his consent for the surgery.

478
00:33:17,695 --> 00:33:18,930
I gave you the consent form.

479
00:33:18,997 --> 00:33:21,632
Like I said. What are you talking about?

480
00:33:21,699 --> 00:33:22,934
Don't play dumb with me.

481
00:33:23,134 --> 00:33:28,139
Professor Torii is getting weak,
and his consciousness was fading.

482
00:33:28,206 --> 00:33:31,509
Therefore, we asked
Mrs. Torii to sign the consent.

483
00:33:34,078 --> 00:33:37,482
- What?
- This is that consent form.

484
00:33:43,755 --> 00:33:46,090
What's this? How can this be?

485
00:33:47,492 --> 00:33:50,828
Professor Torii personally
asked me to operate on him.

486
00:33:52,830 --> 00:33:54,332
Isn't that right, ma'am?

487
00:33:55,833 --> 00:33:59,370
Director, where did you hide
that consent form?

488
00:34:00,905 --> 00:34:01,773
Answer me!

489
00:34:02,240 --> 00:34:06,310
Now, let's have Professor Hijikata
explain the surgical procedure.

490
00:34:07,011 --> 00:34:11,249
Before that, it's picture time, yes?
Let's have you shake hands.

491
00:34:11,616 --> 00:34:14,685
Handshake, please.
Mrs. Torii, handshake, please.

492
00:34:14,752 --> 00:34:15,987
Okay, here we go.

493
00:34:16,220 --> 00:34:17,822
Next, over here, please!

494
00:34:17,955 --> 00:34:19,590
Over here, thank you!

495
00:34:28,933 --> 00:34:31,502
Hey. Did you skip the conference?

496
00:34:33,237 --> 00:34:34,238
No...

497
00:34:40,978 --> 00:34:42,080
What's the matter?

498
00:34:43,147 --> 00:34:45,450
You look like a frog
being watched by a snake.

499
00:34:49,554 --> 00:34:51,656
- Let's go.
- Ma'am.

500
00:34:52,190 --> 00:34:54,392
Professor Torii said Hijikata
was the last guy

501
00:34:54,459 --> 00:34:56,060
he wanted operating on him.

502
00:34:56,527 --> 00:34:59,664
- Please say something.
- Ma'am, let's go.

503
00:35:04,802 --> 00:35:05,803
Dr. Daimon.

504
00:35:07,839 --> 00:35:10,208
I have a message from Director Busujima.

505
00:35:10,908 --> 00:35:13,578
There's still some time left
on your contract,

506
00:35:14,178 --> 00:35:16,314
but he said you don't have
to come in after today.

507
00:35:17,482 --> 00:35:18,749
You mean I'm fired?

508
00:35:20,251 --> 00:35:21,119
Yeah.

509
00:35:22,386 --> 00:35:23,921
I'm sorry I couldn't protect you.

510
00:35:31,896 --> 00:35:35,500
You really haven't changed.

511
00:35:36,534 --> 00:35:39,137
I'll help you find a new place.

512
00:35:40,338 --> 00:35:42,039
Let's go eat when things settle down.

513
00:35:46,644 --> 00:35:47,945
I will not eat.

514
00:35:49,080 --> 00:35:50,248
Michiko!

515
00:36:04,762 --> 00:36:06,164
It can't be helped.

516
00:36:08,266 --> 00:36:10,234
You were always saying...

517
00:36:12,236 --> 00:36:15,273
that you can't survive in the hospital
if you go against the top.

518
00:36:20,945 --> 00:36:23,114
- Did Dr. Daimon get fired?
- Yeah.

519
00:36:24,048 --> 00:36:28,352
Seeing how she went totally
out of control at the open conference.

520
00:36:33,024 --> 00:36:35,426
That talk about
Professor Torii asking Dr. Daimon

521
00:36:36,227 --> 00:36:40,364
to perform the surgery.
What do you think about it?

522
00:36:41,599 --> 00:36:43,467
Demon made it up, of course.

523
00:36:44,268 --> 00:36:46,237
That surgery freak. She probably wanted

524
00:36:46,304 --> 00:36:48,673
to do the living donor liver transplant
no matter what.

525
00:36:48,739 --> 00:36:54,545
But Professor Torii disliked
Professor Hijikata, didn't he?

526
00:36:56,280 --> 00:36:59,550
Entrusting your life
to a junior you dislike.

527
00:37:02,119 --> 00:37:03,955
If that was me, I'd rather die.

528
00:37:09,493 --> 00:37:14,298
But the one who first found
the professor's bile duct cancer

529
00:37:14,732 --> 00:37:19,604
was Dr. Daimon and at the first
conference, she was the only one

530
00:37:19,670 --> 00:37:23,674
<i>who told Professor Torii the truth.</i>

531
00:37:25,209 --> 00:37:27,178
<i>If you had to entrust</i>
<i>your own life to someone,</i>

532
00:37:27,745 --> 00:37:30,481
<i>wouldn't you set aside things</i>
<i>like hospital attachments and career</i>

533
00:37:31,349 --> 00:37:34,151
<i>and entrust your life</i>
<i>to a surgeon like her?</i>

534
00:37:49,467 --> 00:37:53,537
Morimoto. Are you okay?
Are you sure you're not sick?

535
00:37:54,839 --> 00:37:56,340
What's wrong? Catch a cold?

536
00:37:57,074 --> 00:37:59,043
No, it's not that.

537
00:38:06,751 --> 00:38:10,187
What Dr. Daimon said is all true.

538
00:38:11,122 --> 00:38:12,023
What?

539
00:38:14,191 --> 00:38:16,494
The consent form signed
by Professor Torii.

540
00:38:16,927 --> 00:38:18,663
I definitely saw it with my own eyes.

541
00:38:19,964 --> 00:38:21,666
In the Director's office.

542
00:38:24,001 --> 00:38:24,835
Is that true?

543
00:38:26,904 --> 00:38:27,738
Yes.

544
00:38:29,140 --> 00:38:33,544
I see.
So, the snake was Director Busujima.

545
00:38:36,180 --> 00:38:38,049
If you want to survive here,

546
00:38:38,115 --> 00:38:41,919
pretend you never saw this.
Isn't that what you were told?

547
00:38:45,122 --> 00:38:49,327
But knowing him, he probably
got rid of the evidence already.

548
00:38:56,434 --> 00:38:58,969
- We're going to look for it.
- Dr. Kaji.

549
00:39:08,279 --> 00:39:12,116
Of all the ivory towers,
that was the worst, wasn't it?

550
00:39:12,616 --> 00:39:16,454
I'll find you a better hospital next time,
so cheer up.

551
00:39:20,725 --> 00:39:23,027
I'm sorry, at a time like this. <i>Ron.</i>

552
00:39:23,094 --> 00:39:25,262
Seven pairs and<i> dora</i> two.

553
00:39:25,730 --> 00:39:27,932
That's cold.

554
00:39:44,448 --> 00:39:48,352
- It's not here, as we expected.
- I wonder if he burned it already.

555
00:39:52,089 --> 00:39:53,157
Dr. Kaji.

556
00:39:55,226 --> 00:39:58,963
No, I'm not doing it for Demon.
I'm doing it for Professor Torii.

557
00:39:59,029 --> 00:40:00,398
We know that.

558
00:40:00,464 --> 00:40:02,500
But where is it?

559
00:40:03,734 --> 00:40:05,202
- Are you all right?
- Damn, that hurt.

560
00:40:05,269 --> 00:40:06,937
Put it back in place.

561
00:40:16,280 --> 00:40:18,048
- Found it.
- What?

562
00:40:20,651 --> 00:40:22,386
It was right in front of our eyes.

563
00:40:24,388 --> 00:40:26,724
Doctors, what are you doing
at this late hour?

564
00:40:32,163 --> 00:40:36,901
<i>Professor Busujima</i>
<i>will now begin his rounds.</i>

565
00:40:37,868 --> 00:40:40,137
Professor Hijikata will enter
the operating room soon.

566
00:40:40,237 --> 00:40:41,305
CHIEF NURSE
SONOKO CHIBA

567
00:40:41,372 --> 00:40:43,874
The surgery will begin
on schedule at 9:00.

568
00:40:45,109 --> 00:40:47,745
We invited the press
to the observation room as well today.

569
00:40:55,019 --> 00:40:57,922
- Good morning.
- Thanks.

570
00:40:59,523 --> 00:41:00,458
Thank you.

571
00:41:24,682 --> 00:41:27,418
Surgery on the donor
by Professor Hijikata is finished.

572
00:41:27,785 --> 00:41:29,019
He will be here shortly.

573
00:41:29,220 --> 00:41:32,189
The graft is packed in saline
and stored in ice.

574
00:41:34,258 --> 00:41:37,728
- Finally.
- Come. Take a good look.

575
00:41:38,028 --> 00:41:41,932
The surgery built on teacher
and student love is about to begin.

576
00:41:56,447 --> 00:41:57,348
Let's begin.

577
00:41:58,048 --> 00:42:00,451
We will now begin
the living donor liver transplant

578
00:42:00,518 --> 00:42:03,521
of Professor Takashi Tori
by Professor Hijikata.

579
00:42:03,954 --> 00:42:07,057
Blood pressure 104 over 60.
Pulmonary artery catheter

580
00:42:07,124 --> 00:42:08,826
placed in the right interior jugular vein.

581
00:42:08,893 --> 00:42:10,528
- Scalpel.
- Yes.

582
00:42:17,902 --> 00:42:19,303
You, there. Get out of my way.

583
00:42:21,605 --> 00:42:22,773
He's my patient.

584
00:42:25,576 --> 00:42:29,013
- Ms. Daimon.
- It's that doctor again.

585
00:42:29,446 --> 00:42:32,283
Director, what's going on?

586
00:42:32,349 --> 00:42:35,586
Daimon. Stop obstructing
Professor Hijikata's surgery!

587
00:42:35,653 --> 00:42:37,721
Get out of the operating room
this instant!

588
00:42:37,788 --> 00:42:38,656
No way.

589
00:42:40,190 --> 00:42:41,892
Because he's my patient.

590
00:42:42,660 --> 00:42:44,862
You know that better
than anyone else, don't you?

591
00:42:45,563 --> 00:42:46,730
What the hell is going on?

592
00:42:54,204 --> 00:42:56,173
- You're late, Morimoto.
- My apologies.

593
00:42:56,240 --> 00:42:59,977
- Third assistant, I hope you brought it.
- Yes.

594
00:43:01,078 --> 00:43:03,514
- It?
- This.

595
00:43:05,349 --> 00:43:07,985
It's signed by Professor Torii
when he was still conscious.

596
00:43:11,789 --> 00:43:13,023
It can't be.

597
00:43:13,657 --> 00:43:15,726
It's Professor Torii's handwriting.

598
00:43:17,828 --> 00:43:20,397
- You're the primary surgeon?
- Isn't that what I told you?

599
00:43:20,464 --> 00:43:22,132
Director. What does this mean?

600
00:43:24,401 --> 00:43:26,337
Michiko Daimon...

601
00:43:26,403 --> 00:43:29,239
Director Busujima, it's always
a pleasure working with you.

602
00:43:29,306 --> 00:43:35,145
Here's a melon for you.
But isn't it too harsh to fire her?

603
00:43:35,212 --> 00:43:38,315
Here you go, everyone.
A copy of the consent form.

604
00:43:38,382 --> 00:43:40,751
Here you go!

605
00:43:48,225 --> 00:43:49,693
But why?

606
00:43:50,861 --> 00:43:52,463
Why did Professor Torii choose you,

607
00:43:52,830 --> 00:43:55,833
who isn't a professor or an associate,
or a member of the medical staff

608
00:43:55,933 --> 00:43:57,001
to be his primary surgeon?

609
00:43:58,469 --> 00:44:00,938
Because I will not fail.

610
00:44:09,013 --> 00:44:11,749
Professor Hijikata. You're in her way.
Will you please get out?

611
00:44:12,116 --> 00:44:15,619
Unless you want to assist.
Third assistants only do suction.

612
00:44:19,556 --> 00:44:20,858
I'll take my leave.

613
00:44:27,598 --> 00:44:31,869
Let's begin now. We will now begin
the living donor liver transplant

614
00:44:31,935 --> 00:44:35,639
on Professor Torii
by freelancer Michiko Daimon.

615
00:44:36,707 --> 00:44:38,075
- Scalpel.
- Yes.

616
00:44:55,559 --> 00:44:56,760
- Metzen.
- Yes.

617
00:45:12,943 --> 00:45:13,777
All right.

618
00:45:14,845 --> 00:45:16,480
- Get the retractor ready.
- Yes.

619
00:45:16,580 --> 00:45:17,715
Subtitle translation by Kelly True

620
00:45:18,449 --> 00:45:19,349
FINAL EPISODE

621
00:45:19,416 --> 00:45:21,418
- We'll stop his heart.
- That's impossible.

622
00:45:21,485 --> 00:45:23,654
- Someone, stop Dr. Daimon!
- I will not fail.

623
00:45:23,721 --> 00:45:24,555
FAREWELL MICHIKO DAIMON

624
00:45:24,621 --> 00:45:26,623
Surgery Department II
will be dissolved immediately.

625
00:45:26,690 --> 00:45:29,193
<i>Evil doctors who place</i>
<i>human lives on a scale.</i>

626
00:45:29,259 --> 00:45:32,463
It can't be. The real Doctor X is...
